{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Close attempt — AC1-AC4 verified and ticked; AC5 (LIVE VALIDATION) FAILS: merged but NOT deployed\n\nMerge SHA: **`25fd2cf6dd75`** (\"Stop the sibling edge surfaces downgrading\", Gerrit change 2348),\nreachable from `origin/main` (`25ea12c200ae`). Verified in a fresh worktree detached at\n`25ea12c200ae`: `git merge-base --is-ancestor 25fd2cf6dd75 HEAD` -> true.\n\n**The ticket cannot be closed.** The code landed; the running system was never updated. Every\nlive probe below reproduces the ORIGINAL pre-fix downgrade, today.\n\n---\n\n### AC5 — LIVE VALIDATION: **NOT MET**\n\nUnauthenticated probes of the deployed edge, no credential transmitted:\n\n```\n$ curl -sS -o /dev/null -D - https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/review/health/\nHTTP/2 307\nlocation: http://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/health\nstrict-transport-security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains\n\n$ curl -sS -o /dev/null -D - https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/review/webhook/\nHTTP/2 307\nlocation: http://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/webhook\n\n$ curl -sS -o /dev/null -D - https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/review/rerun/\nHTTP/2 307\nlocation: http://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/rerun\n\n$ curl -sS -o /dev/null -D - https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/opcert/jobs/\nHTTP/2 403          (no Location — nginx X-Opcert-Guard rejects before proxying)\n\n$ curl -sS -o /dev/null -D - https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/opcert/health/\nHTTP/2 403          (no Location — same guard)\n\n$ curl -sS -o /dev/null -D - https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/settings\nHTTP/2 302\nlocation: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/settings/\n\n$ curl -sS -o /dev/null -D - https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/Documentation\nHTTP/2 302\nlocation: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/Documentation/index.html\n```\n\n**Liveness anchors — each probe is proven to have reached the surface under test, so no result\nhere is the vacuous \"no Location because nothing happened\".**\n\n- `/review/` — anchored by an authentic review-bot application response, not a generic 404:\n  ```\n  $ curl -sS -D - https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/review/health\n  HTTP/2 200\n  server: nginx/1.30.2\n  content-type: application/json\n  {\"status\":\"ok\",\"in_flight\":2,\"queue_depth\":3}\n  ```\n  That body is the review-bot's own health payload. The trailing-slash variant then ELICITS an\n  actual redirect, so there IS a `Location` header to inspect — and it is `http://`. This\n  distinguishes \"correctly rewritten\" from \"no redirect happened\": a redirect happened, and it\n  downgraded.\n- Gerrit `location /` — anchored by two real 302s carrying absolute same-host Locations\n  (`/settings`, `/Documentation`), both already `https` from `canonicalWebUrl`.\n- Control, to prove a generic miss looks different: `GET /zzz-nonexistent-surface/` -> `HTTP/2\n  404`, no Location. None of the surfaces above returned that shape.\n- `/opcert/` — the 403 is nginx's own fail-closed `X-Opcert-Guard` rejection, i.e. a recognisable\n  response FROM the `/opcert/` location block rather than a fallthrough 404. **But it is\n  explicitly NOT a pass**: nginx never proxies, so the `proxy_redirect` backstop under test never\n  runs. Unauthenticated `/opcert/` cannot validate this criterion in either direction; it is\n  untestable at this privilege posture, not satisfied by it.\n\n### Why AC5 fails: the change merged but was never deployed\n\nRead-only inspection of box `i-00880b2c7f13527c5` (`us-east-1`, via `aws ssm send-command`\nrunning only `grep` / `ls` / `docker inspect` — no write, no reload, no restart):\n\n```\n$ grep -n proxy_redirect /etc/nginx/conf.d/rebar.conf\n165:        # level, NOT server level: proxy_redirect defaults to `default`, which is derived\n168:        proxy_redirect http://$host/ https://$host/;\n169:        proxy_redirect http://rebar_mcp/ https://$host/;\n184:        proxy_redirect http://$host/ https://$host/;\n185:        proxy_redirect http://rebar_mcp/ https://$host/;\n203:        proxy_redirect http://$host/ https://$host/;\n204:        proxy_redirect http://rebar_mcp/ https://$host/;\n\n$ ls -la /etc/nginx/conf.d/\n-rw-r--r--. 1 root root 12618 Aug 27 22:05 rebar.conf\n```\n\nThe running config carries **only 79b2's three MCP `rebar_mcp` rules**. None of a61d's six new\nsibling rules — the `/review/` `127.0.0.1:${REVIEW_BOT_PORT}` pair, the `/opcert/` `127.0.0.1:8090`\npair, the Gerrit `127.0.0.1:8080` pair, nor any of the three restated `proxy_redirect default;`\nlines — is present. The file is dated **Aug 27 22:05**; a61d merged **Aug 28 15:16**.\n\nThe root-cause layer is equally absent:\n\n```\n$ docker inspect compose-review-bot-1 --format '{{range .Config.Env}}{{println .}}{{end}}' | grep -i FORWARDED\n(no match)\n$ docker inspect compose-opcert-1 --format '{{range .Config.Env}}{{println .}}{{end}}' | grep -i FORWARDED\n(no match)\n```\n\nNeither container carries `FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS`, so uvicorn still defaults to `\"127.0.0.1\"`,\nstill distrusts the docker-bridge peer, still drops `X-Forwarded-Proto: https`, and Starlette\nstill builds `http://` absolute URLs — exactly the confirmed mechanism in the RCA comment.\n\nContainers are `compose-review-bot-1 Up About an hour`, `compose-opcert-1 Up 24 hours`, i.e. the\nrestart the compose change needs has not happened either. Per the deploy note on the previous\ncomment, `review-bot` and `opcert` need a container restart and nginx needs a config\nrender + reload; neither occurred.\n\nNote this is the `waspy-piecemeal-queenconch` failure mode's cousin: a pipeline reporting success\nis not evidence of a redeploy. Here the running artefacts were read directly and they are stale.\n\n---\n\n### AC1 — MET (ticked)\n\nEstablished and recorded for all three surfaces, in the Phase-1-exit RCA comment above, by\ninspecting how each app builds redirects and its proxy-headers trust boundary:\n\n- `/review/` **CAN** emit an absolute `http://` Location — reproduced live above.\n- `/opcert/` **CAN** — same mechanism: `FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS` is set for the `mcp` service only\n  (`infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`), unset for `review-bot` and `opcert`; both are published on\n  host loopback so nginx connects from the bridge gateway and is untrusted. Confirmed again today\n  against the live containers (`docker inspect` output above).\n- Gerrit `location /` **CAN** emit absolute same-host Locations but does **not** downgrade — it\n  builds them from `canonicalWebUrl = https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/`\n  (`infra/compose/gerrit.config:14`). Confirmed live: `/settings` and `/Documentation` both 302 to\n  `https://`. Its guarantee rests on a config value nothing at the edge enforces, which is why it\n  still gets the backstop.\n\n### AC2 — MET (ticked)\n\n`infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template` at `25fd2cf6dd75` carries, per-location and never server-level:\n\n```\n/review/  :117 proxy_redirect default;\n          :118 proxy_redirect http://$host/ https://$host/;\n          :119 proxy_redirect http://127.0.0.1:${REVIEW_BOT_PORT}/ https://$host/;\n/opcert/  :146 proxy_redirect default;\n          :147 proxy_redirect http://$host/ https://$host/;\n          :148 proxy_redirect http://127.0.0.1:8090/ https://$host/;\nGerrit /  :289 proxy_redirect default;\n          :290 proxy_redirect http://$host/ https://$host/;\n          :291 proxy_redirect http://127.0.0.1:8080/ https://$host/;\n```\n\nStructural test over the RENDERED template:\n`tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py::test_nginx_upgrades_any_plaintext_location_on_the_sibling_surfaces`\nplus `test_compose_sibling_services_trust_the_edge_forwarded_proto[review-bot]` and `[opcert]`.\nRe-run today in a fresh worktree at `25ea12c200ae`: **7 passed, 45 deselected**.\n\n### AC3 — MET (ticked)\n\n`proxy_redirect default;` is restated FIRST in each of the three blocks (`:117`, `:146`, `:289`),\nbefore any explicit rule, so nginx does not drop the implicit default and `/review/`'s\nprefix-stripping rewrite survives. Pinned by\n`test_nginx_sibling_surfaces_restate_the_default_proxy_redirect`, which asserts `default` is both\npresent AND first — passing.\n\n### AC4 — MET (ticked)\n\n`proxy_redirect` rewrites only the `Location`/`Refresh` **response** headers; it is not a\n`rewrite` and adds no URI path to `proxy_pass`, so it cannot touch the request URI that Gerrit's\n`%2F`-safe proxying depends on (standing constraint at `rebar.conf.template:245-252`). Pinned by\n`test_nginx_gerrit_location_still_has_no_rewrite_and_no_proxy_pass_path`, which fails if the\nbackstop is ever turned into a `rewrite` or a path is added to Gerrit's `proxy_pass` — passing.\nCorroborated live (current, pre-deploy edge): an encoded-slash Gerrit path proxies correctly —\n`GET /projects/rebar/branches/refs%2Fheads%2Fmain` -> `HTTP/2 200`.\n\n---\n\n### Blocked — escalating rather than forcing\n\nTicket stays `in_progress`. The close gate is correct to refuse: AC5 is a genuine, currently\nfalse assertion about the deployed system. Clearing it requires a **deploy** — rendering the\ntemplate and reloading nginx, and recreating `review-bot`/`opcert` with the new env — which is a\nmutation of a shared box and needs operator approval before an agent performs it. No `--force`\nwas used and no gate was bypassed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787958516109029001,"uuid":"0348360f-f29b-4a23-ada7-4e99dcd87deb"}